A||||6||Tom88gt||88 front wheel bearings?||||5||
Z||000000||Tom88gt||05-19-2001||03:48 PM||||I think my front wheel bearing went out today.  I was driving and everytime I turn to the right the left front wheel squeals.  Kinda like a fan belt squeal but not as loud.  I turned off the AC and vents just to make sure.  I'm pretty sure it is the wheel bearing.  <P>How do you replace it?  I can't find the 1988 sealed hub discussed anywhere in the Haynes manual.  I'm sure it's not too hard.  Just looking for some insight.<P>Thanks,<BR>Tom||||reg||5
Z||000001||88formula||05-19-2001||04:12 PM||||Are you sure it’s not the brake sensor that is rubbing against the rotor? When the brake pads wear out a metal tab rubs against the rotor and it squeals, usually when you are turning. <P>I have not been able to find a replacement bearing.<BR><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_logo_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||fiero56||05-19-2001||04:36 PM||||Timken still makes the setup. I don't have the part number in front of me(its on my other 'puter), but will post it later today if no-one else does.<P>Found it on this one too <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">.<P>Timken part #: 513040<BR>This number can be ordered under the "Timken" or "BCA/Federal Mogul" brand name.<p>[This message has been edited by fiero56 (edited 05-19-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||rodmcneill||05-19-2001||08:51 PM||||fiero56, is this part # just the bearing itself or the complete hub assembly? How difficult is it to change a bearing in a hub assemble? Just press out, press in?||||reg||5
Z||000004||Bob Englert||05-19-2001||08:56 PM||||The hub assembly is not designed to be user servicable.  You just replace the entire assembly.  It is actually very easy to replace.  <BR><P>------------------<BR>Bob<BR>2 - 87 GT's<BR>85 SE 4 cyl||||reg||1
Z||000005||Will||05-19-2001||10:54 PM||||Obviously, you need to do the 3-9 and 12-6 o'clock checks before you replace the bearing.<P>Replaceing the bearing is <I>supposed</I> to be easy. I replaced one, and had to hit it bloody hard to knock it loose from the hub carrier. Chipped the end of a prybar in the process. The new one went in easily, however.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000006||Tom88gt||06-09-2001||11:04 AM||||Got the left front wheel off and the brake wear sensor was up against the rotor.  New set of pads and no squeal!!!  Cleaned and painted the front calipers with gloss red engine paint while the wheels were off.  Not too visible through the lace wheels but still a nice touch.||||reg||7
